%% UC01 Submit reservation - design sequence diagram (behind the load balancer)
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor B as Borrower
  participant LB as nginx LB
  participant SEC as Security<br/>filters
  participant C as Reservation<br/>Controller
  participant S as Reservation<br/>Service
  participant RR as Reservation<br/>Rules
  participant R as Reservation<br/>Repository
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant EV as Event<br/>Publisher
  B->>LB: POST /api/v1/reservations<br/>JSESSIONID cookie, X-XSRF-TOKEN
  LB->>SEC: least_conn → app-k
  SEC->>DB: load session (spring_session)
  SEC->>SEC: CSRF + session_version
  SEC->>C: create(request, principal)
  C->>S: submit(requesterId, request)
  Note over S: @PreAuthorize BORROWER<br/>@Transactional begin
  S->>R: lockEquipment(id)
  R->>DB: SELECT … FOR UPDATE
  alt retired / under maintenance / open fault
    S-->>C: EquipmentUnavailable 409
  end
  S->>R: lockRequesterAccountStatus()
  S->>R: countOpen(), hasOverdueLoan()
  S->>RR: evaluate(ruleContext)
  RR-->>S: violations
  alt violations not empty
    S-->>C: RulesBroken 422
  end
  S->>R: overlapsHeldSlot(), insert(…)
  R->>DB: INSERT reservation
  alt concurrent overlap
    DB-->>R: 23P01 exclusion violation
    S-->>C: SlotTaken 409
  end
  S->>R: audit(RESERVATION_SUBMIT)
  S->>EV: ReservationSubmitted
  EV->>DB: queue notification (same tx)
  Note over S,DB: COMMIT
  S-->>C: Reservation
  C-->>B: 201 Created
